    "faq.label":"FAQ","faq.title":"Frequently asked questions","faq.lead":"Answers to the most important questions about Meyssens and digital civic participation.",
    "faq.q1":"Do we need our own IT infrastructure?","faq.a1":"No. Meyssens is a fully managed service. We take care of hosting, updates, backups and security. Your municipality needs no server infrastructure of its own and no in-house IT expertise.",
    "faq.q2":"Is a public tender required?","faq.a2":"For small contracts, direct award is often possible; the thresholds depend on your municipality and your country, and we are happy to clarify this with you in a conversation.",
    "faq.q3":"What is Decidim, and why does Meyssens build on it?","faq.a3":"Meyssens is based on Decidim, an open-source platform used by cities worldwide. The source code is open, there is no vendor lock-in, and your data can be exported at any time.",
    "faq.q4":"How long does setup take?","faq.a4":"Launch usually takes place within a few weeks. After a consultation call, we set up the platform with your logo, colours and content. We then train your team and support you through the official launch.",
    "faq.q5":"Which languages are supported?","faq.a5":"The platform supports German, French and Italian. Multilingual municipalities can run the platform entirely in several languages.",
    "faq.q6":"How secure is our residents' data?","faq.a6":"Hosting takes place exclusively in Switzerland, in a data centre in Zurich. Data protection in line with GDPR requirements, data processing agreement on request. The platform complies with the Swiss Data Protection Act (DSG). Data is never passed to third parties or used for advertising.",
    "faq.q7":"What happens to our data if we cancel?","faq.a7":"You receive all your data in a standardised format (export). Since Decidim is open source, you can keep running the platform yourself or switch providers at any time. There is no lock-in.",
    "faq.q9":"Do you also work with cities and municipalities in Germany?","faq.a9":"Yes. Meyssens was developed in Switzerland and is open to cities and municipalities in Germany, currently especially in Baden-Württemberg. Billing is in euros.","faq.q10":"Does the GDPR apply to German municipalities, and is hosting in Switzerland permitted?","faq.a10":"Data protection in line with GDPR requirements, data processing agreement on request. The European Commission has recognised Switzerland as providing an adequate level of data protection, so data may be transferred to Switzerland without additional safeguards. We are happy to clarify details in a conversation.","faq.q8":"How many residents is the platform suitable for?","faq.a8":"Meyssens suits municipalities of any size — from small municipalities with under 5,000 residents to cities and cantons.",
    "about.label":"About us","about.title":"Your Swiss partner for digital participation","about.role":"Founder, Meyssens",
    "about.card":"Meyssens was founded with a clear mission: to give cities and municipalities access to modern digital civic participation — without major technical overhead and at a fixed price of €4,900 per year for municipalities with up to 5,000 inhabitants, with no setup fees.",
    "about.body":"We build on <a href=\"https://decidim.org\" target=\"_blank\" style=\"color:var(--blue);text-decoration:none;font-weight:500\">Decidim</a>, an open-source platform used by cities worldwide. As a Swiss provider, we know the particularities of municipal administrations in the German-speaking region.",
    "about.quote":"\u201cEvery municipality deserves a modern platform that truly involves its residents.\u201d",
